<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:64:octeon2:default">
<!--
    kuna octeoneffects: an Octeon atomic or load-linked accesses memory through
    its address operand, but a user operation has no memory effect of its own,
    so a store before it was forwarded past it or dropped. Upstream's MIPS spec
    lifts ll/sc as a plain load/store and sync as SYNC(n); `off` restores that.

    update  (0x1000): ori a0,zero,0x2000; daddiu a1,zero,7; sd a1,0(a0);
                      laad zero,(a0),a1; ld v0,0(a0); jr ra; nop
    barrier (0x1100): the same with syncw in place of laad
    spill   (0x1200): daddiu sp,sp,-16; sd a0,8(sp); syncw; ld v0,8(sp);
                      jr ra; daddiu sp,sp,16
    reserve (0x1300): the same as update with sc a2,0(a0) in place of laad
    linked  (0x1400): ori a0,zero,0x2000; sd a1,0(a0); lld t0,0(a0);
                      sd zero,0(a0); jr ra; or v0,t0,zero
    snapshot (0x1500): ld v0,0(a0); saad a1,(a0); jr ra; nop
    zero_neighbor (0x1600): daddiu sp,sp,-32; sd a1,8(sp);
                      daddiu a0,sp,16; zcb (a0); ld v0,8(sp);
                      jr ra; daddiu sp,sp,32
    ordered_snapshot (0x1700): ld v0,0(a0); syncw; jr ra; nop
    zero_neighbor_transient (0x1800): as zero_neighbor, but offset 24 and zcbt
    Source/build provenance: tests/fixtures/octeon-atomics/memory.S,
    build.py and provenance.json (GNU as -EB -64 -march=octeon2).

    Stage: P2 lift (callother fixups) and P3 dataflow (heritage guards).
    Three passes: off (update returns the stored 7; barrier and reserve lift
    as upstream does), atomic (the default: update rereads, the store linked
    reads stays, a barrier writes nothing so barrier returns 7 and the spill
    stays a value), ordered (barrier rereads too).

    Assert #1: `return 7;` for update and barrier under off, barrier under atomic.
    Assert #2: the spill across syncw stays the incoming value under atomic.
    Assert #3: atomic and ordered keep the barrier as octeon_syncw.
    Assert #4: off lifts syncw as upstream's SYNC(4).
    Assert #5: off lifts sc as upstream's plain store into the reloaded word.
    Assert #6: atomic keeps the store the load-linked reads.
    Assert #7: atomic and ordered capture the pointer load before the atomic.
    Assert #8: ordered captures a pointer load before the barrier too.
    Assert #9: off retains opaque-operation load motion as a control.
    Assert #10: only off forwards a neighboring stack value past ZCB/ZCBT.
    Assert #11: full-block guards keep the neighboring stores before zeroing.
-->
